DATASET: BHARATTHERMAL-1, NOT YET LICENSED FOR REDISTRIBUTION

The dataset is not covered by either licence above and is not released. It is held
for a research publication in preparation.

The reason is specific rather than procedural. The feature set contains a column
copied from an OpenStreetMap attribute and a column computed against OpenStreetMap
geometry. OpenStreetMap is licensed ODbL 1.0, which requires share alike on a
Derivative Database but only attribution on a Produced Work. Which of the two this
dataset constitutes has not been determined, and the answer decides whether it can
be released under CC BY 4.0 at all.

The position is stated here rather than assumed in either direction, and the
dataset stays unreleased until it is settled with qualified advice.

Separately, the EOG gas flare catalogue used during construction permits
attribution but does not confirm redistribution. Values derived from it are
published only as coarse distance bands, because exact distances from many known
points can be trilaterated back to the catalogue.


UPSTREAM SOURCES AND THEIR TERMS

  NASA FIRMS                     active fire detections, free and open,
                                 attribution requested
  OpenStreetMap                  ODbL 1.0, attribution and share alike on a
                                 derivative database
